"## Summary\n\nNetlab follow-up 34: session launched 13:18 EST on 2026-11-03 on #429's roadmap row `1b87ab32`, and delivered at 13:57. One continuation, on the same thread, ran from 14:00 to 14:12.\n- **Model:** codex `gpt-6-astra`.\n- **Size:** 7 commits and 769 owned files, +806,727/\u221210:\n  - five production files in `node/enforce/`: `render_nft.go`, `parse_nft.go` and `verify.go`, and the new `verify_mss.go` and `verify_pmtu.go`;\n  - their tests: two new files, three adjusted test files and two goldens;\n  - one netlab scenario and two scripts;\n  - the agent's test translator, `node/agent/followup12_test.go`, test-only;\n  - the dated record, and 752 evidence files under `docs/poc/G2-followup34-evidence/`.\n- **Checks:**\n  - merge-tree clean on current `main`; prepush-scan clean; owned-check passes.\n  - The orchestrator merged this branch into current `main` on a scratch tree, and reran these there under its own reservation. All pass:\n    - the node and installer consumer gate, `go test -count=1 ./node/... ./packaging/installer/...`;\n    - `go test -count=1 ./tests/handover/...`;\n    - the offline tests in `tests/e2e/at/...` and `tests/netlab/...`, and the committed-evidence tests in `tests/netlab` and `tests/e2e`;\n    - `go vet ./node/...`, gofmt and `git diff --check`.\n- **Scope:** no MTU, dependency or pin change. No reservation and no timing comparison.\n\n**The orchestrator's reading.**\n- **D-146, the TCP MSS clamp.**\n  - **The value:** 1160, for both underlay families. Through a 1280-byte receiving link, the largest inner packet is 1216 over IPv4 and 1200 over IPv6, after WireGuard's header, tag and 16-byte padding. Inner 1200 gives outer 1260 over IPv4 and 1280 over IPv6.\n  - **When:** only on SYN, SYN-ACK included, and only when an existing MSS option exceeds 1160. A missing option or a smaller value is untouched. It acts on new handshakes.\n  - **Where:** one non-verdict clamp just before each admitted address's general upload accept, and one just before its download accept.\n    - The clamps have no counter or priority.\n    - Every other rule keeps its order and expression. DNS and probe accepts get no clamp.\n- **D-147, RELATED fragmentation-needed.**\n  - **The rule:** three accepts per admitted address. They sit before the download source-deny drops, and after the membership, established / related and DNS rules. Each matches:\n    - a source in `resolver_v4`, `denied_v4` or `host_v4`;\n    - exactly the admitted address as destination;\n    - conntrack RELATED;\n    - ICMP type 3, code 4.\n  - **Metering:** each uses the device's existing download counter and priority. The first match accepts, so overlapping sets cannot double-count.\n  - **What it does not grant:** upload reachability, a probe exception, unsolicited downloads, any other ICMP type or code, or IPv6 forwarding.\n- **Enforcement:** the parser accepts only the new bounded shapes.\n  - The live verifier requires their complete matches, values, counters, priorities, cardinality and placement.\n  - Mutated copies and foreign mangle statements fail verification, `nftrace` included.\n- **The lab evidence,** on a fixed IPv4 underlay:\n  - **Receive-only 1280, TCP:**\n    - the download went from 0 of 64,064 bytes on unchanged `main` to 64,064 bytes with the rules; the upload completed both times;\n    - member SYN MSS 1380 \u2192 1160 and origin SYN-ACK 1460 \u2192 1160, while a smaller 1000 stayed 1000.\n  - **Receive-only 1280, UDP:** the reply is still lost, as D-146 records. QUIC is not tested, because the lab has no QUIC client.\n  - **A private router with MTU 1000 on the upload path:**\n    - the TCP upload went from 0 bytes and a timeout, with PMTU stuck at 1420, to 64,064 bytes with PMTU 1000 learned;\n    - its fragmentation-needed errors: 15 dropped at `ctdenyd` on `main`; with the rules, 10 forwarded and counted once, as 5,760 download IP bytes in the member's class.\n  - **Still dropped:**\n    - time-exceeded, at `ctdenyd`;\n    - an unsolicited fragmentation-needed, at `ctinv`;\n    - the member's ping to the router, at `ctdeny`, with no upload usage.\n  - **Accounting:** usage deltas match independent node-egress captures exactly, in each direction.\n- **Gates:** the full netlab gate passes, and so do all 13 ordinary agent scenarios, D-087 / D-104 included.\n- **Gate 3a failed first, because of the orchestrator's brief.** The unchanged consumer command failed 22 top-level `node/agent` fixture tests, because the agent's test translator could not parse the new statements.\n  - **Why:** the brief said consumers had to pass \"without edits\". That repeated the wording follow-up 32 had needed clarified. The two agent fixture files are netlab's listed ownership exceptions.\n  - **Continuation 1** extended the translator faithfully, in `followup12_test.go` only, to cover:\n    - the SYN flag test;\n    - the maxseg comparison and mangle;\n    - ICMP type and code;\n    - the singleton RELATED `in` operator;\n    - numeric priorities.\n  - **A new negative test** checks that an unknown or malformed statement still fails its batch atomically.\n  - **The consumer gate then passed,** and gates 4 to 9 were rerun. The continuation changed no production file, and the first failure stays in the evidence.\n- **Not verified here:** the IPv6 underlay, native reconnects, relay and real platforms. Historical F8-02 rows stay failed.\n- **This merge starts two reruns, netlab's hand-offs:**\n  - **Members 18:** AT09's receive-only MTU 1280 rows on the clamp, with endpoint MSS, outer sizes and no-PTB evidence for each underlay family.\n    - **The orchestrator's reading of D-146** (the owner may overturn it): a receive-only TCP row passes only with that evidence.\n  - **Isolation 19:** AT13's D-147 exception across resolver, denied and host sources, with exact download usage, priority and its negatives.\n- **Routed to the next handover:**\n  - the README's \"RELATED ICMP outer source\" row;\n  - the operator guide's traceroute paragraph;\n  - D-146's and D-147's register entries, with their limits.\n"
